        "headingId": 1088,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153599,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> malignant rhabdoid tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153600,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153601,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These sarcomas usually arise in the uterine corpus; occasional cases have been reported in the uterine cervix.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153602,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with signs or symptoms resulting from a uterine mass, such as vaginal bleeding, or complications of pelvic or distant spread. Many patients are at an advanced stage at the time of diagnosis {29700418; 31567195}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153603,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SMARC-deficient uterine sarcomas are extremely rare (&lt;&nbsp;1% of uterine mesenchymal tumours) and tend to occur in premenopausal women (median age: 42&nbsp;years, range: 24&ndash;60&nbsp;years) {31190001; 31567195}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153604,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153605,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Somatic and/or germline inactivating alterations in <em>SMARCA4</em> underlie these tumours {29700418; 31190001; 31567195; 31954538}. A single case with <em>SMARCB1</em> inactivation has been reported {31567195}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153606,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are large (median: 106&nbsp;mm, range: 55&ndash;255&nbsp;mm) uterine masses with a tan-pink to white, soft, cut surface that may have haemorrhage and necrosis {31190001; 31567195}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153607,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours grow as sheets, nests, and cords of monomorphic, medium to large, frequently rhabdoid, epithelioid cells with prominent nucleoli. A subset consists of smaller epithelioid cells or contains a spindled component. Extracellular matrix may be hyalinized, myxohyaline, or occasionally myxoid. Mitotic activity is brisk (mean: 8&nbsp;mitoses/mm<sup>2</sup>). Lymphovascular invasion, necrosis, and haemorrhage are frequently seen. In some tumours, entrapped and distorted benign endometrial or endocervical glands impart a phyllodes-like appearance.</p>\r\n<p>SMARC-deficient uterine sarcomas demonstrate immunohistochemical loss of SMARCA4 (BRG1) or <em>SMARCB1</em> (INI1) expression. They are negative for epithelial markers or exhibit staining of only rare cells; expression of melanocytic and myogenic markers is absent.</p>\r\n<p>The main differential diagnosis is undifferentiated endometrial carcinoma, which tends to occur in older women, is often microsatellite unstable, harbours mutations in <em>TP53, PIK3CA, PTEN, </em>and <em>CTNNB1</em>, and has a distinct methylation profile {31567195; 35218556}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153608,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153609,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours harbour biallelic inactivating alterations in <em>SMARCA4</em> or <em>SMARCB1</em> in the absence of other molecular alterations and exhibit relatively few copy-number alterations {31567195; 35218556}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153610,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> undifferentiated epithelioid to rhabdoid neoplasm with loss of SMARCA4 (BRG1) or SMARCB1 (INI1) expression; intact mismatch repair immunohistochemistry.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> <em>SMARCA4 </em>or <em>SMARCB1</em> inactivation; exclusion of molecular alterations associated with undifferentiated carcinoma (mutations in <em>TP53, PIK3CA, PTEN, </em>or <em>CTNNB1</em>)<em>.</em></p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153611,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>SMARC-deficient uterine sarcomas are staged as uterine sarcomas using the FIGO, the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC), and the American Joint Committee on Cancer (AJCC) systems.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 153612,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 235,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours appear to be uniformly fatal with a median survival of 9&nbsp;months {31567195}. Prognostic features have not been identified.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T15:11:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]